Record Identity (DID) {#chapter-identity}
=====================================

## Definition ## {#section-identity-definition}

Every [=Record=] MUST possess a globally unique, permanent <dfn>Identity</dfn>.

This identity:

- MUST be independent of the physical storage location of the [=Record=]
- MUST be independent of the organisation managing the [=Record=]
- MUST NOT be changed after the [=Record=] has been created
- MUST remain valid without change even after a system migration
- MUST be machine-resolvable (a resolver MUST be able to retrieve the DID document from the identity)


## DID Format ## {#section-did-format}

The identity of a [=Record=] MUST be expressed as a Decentralized Identifier (DID) in accordance with [[DID-CORE]].

**Normative format:**
`did:rwp:<namespace>:<recordId>[:<versionHash>][:<contentHash>]`

The `<namespace>` component identifies the resolution scope of the DID.
The `<recordId>` component identifies a Record within that scope.
The `<versionHash>` component MUST NOT be part of the identity a Record, identifies a specific version of the Record.
The `<contentHash>` component MUST NOT be part of the identity a Record, identifies a specific content within the version.


<table class="data">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Component</th><th>Requirement Level</th><th>Encoding</th><th>Constraints</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>did:rwp:</code></td>
      <td>MUST</td>
      <td>fixed, lowercase</td>
      <td>MUST be prefixed exactly as shown; no uppercase variants permitted</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>&lt;namespace&gt;</code></td>
      <td>MUST</td>
      <td>UUIDv4 (global) or implementation-defined (local)</td>
      <td>See below, globally or locally resolvable RWP DIDs</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>&lt;recordId&gt;</code></td>
      <td>MUST</td>
      <td>UUIDv4 (global) or implementation-defined (local)</td>
      <td>See below, globally or locally resolvable RWP DIDs</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>&lt;versionHash&gt;</code></td>
      <td>MAY (optional)</td>
      <td>64 lowercase hex characters</td>
      <td>MUST NOT carry an algorithm prefix; MUST NOT be treated as part of DID identity; resolver behaviour undefined</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>&lt;contentHash&gt;</code></td>
      <td>MAY (optional)</td>
      <td>64 lowercase hex characters</td>
      <td>MUST NOT carry an algorithm prefix; MUST NOT be treated as part of DID identity; resolver behaviour undefined</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Further segments</td>
      <td>MUST NOT (global); MAY (local)</td>
      <td>---</td>
      <td>Global: implementations MUST assume that no additional segments exist. Local: entirely implementation-defined, no constraint by this specification</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

